From: SacredTrees <121399723+SacredTrees@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 11:40:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] amigaos: soft-float m68040 does not link libm881

`-m68040` without `-m68881` generates the soft-float ABI, with floating
values in integer registers.  Linking libnix's libm881 in that case returns
values in fp0 and also makes the result unusable on an LC/EC040.

Keep libm020 for every 68040 build, but add libm881 only when hard float is
explicitly requested (or for the 68060/68080 targets, which already imply
it).  This makes the temporary m68k-soft-m68040.specs override unnecessary
in a toolchain containing the fix.
---
 gcc/config/m68k/m68kamigaos.h | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/gcc/config/m68k/m68kamigaos.h b/gcc/config/m68k/m68kamigaos.h
index 556e056d3d6..01a8bc73757 100644
--- a/gcc/config/m68k/m68kamigaos.h
+++ b/gcc/config/m68k/m68kamigaos.h
@@ -552,7 +552,7 @@ along with GCC; see the file COPYING3.  If not see
 
 #define LINK_CPU_SPEC \
   "%{m6802*|mc6802*|m6803*|m6804*|m6806*|m6808*|mcpu=6802*|mcpu=6803*|mcpu=6804*|mcpu=6806*|mcpu=6808*:-fl libm020} " \
-  "%{mhard-float|m68881|mcpu=6804*|mcpu=6806*|mcpu=6808*:-fl libm881}"
+  "%{mhard-float|m68881|mcpu=6806*|mcpu=6808*:-fl libm881}"
 
 #ifdef TARGET_AMIGAOS_VASM
 #define LINK_COMMAND_SPEC \
-- 
